 *   language_version 0.23. Comment on the sample: "sealed ledger values
 *   cannot be changed after constructor execution". The sample sets
 *   `export sealed ledger organizer` only in the constructor, then
 *   circuits compare `organizer == pubKey` where pubKey is
 *   persistentHash of a witness secret and a domain pad. It does not
 *   call ownPublicKey().
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/compact/smart-contract-security
 *   "Do not use ownPublicKey() for verification of the caller."
 *   https://docs.midnight.network/guides/security-best-practices
 *   ownPublicKey() is a witness; assert(ownPublicKey().bytes == owner)
 *   compares two prover-controlled values.
